9:Two deliberate choices:
10:
11:- The ledger is per-channel, not global. Two channels are two audiences;
12:  an item one of them received tells us nothing about the other.
13:- Rows are written only after a successful send. If a webhook is down the
14:  run dies with DeliveryError (see channels.py) and nothing is recorded,
15:  so the next tick retries the batch — including items that had already
16:  gone out to an earlier channel this run.
17:
18:History is kept rather than deleted so "did X ever reach channel Y?" stays
19:answerable, and because `item_key` deduplicates per distinct story the
20:table grows by items-per-day, not items-per-tick (tens of rows a day).
21:
22:The pre-2026 schema had an `items` archive table that nothing read; new
23:databases simply do not have it.
